      "taskDescription": "<b>Samira:</b> That first search result already looks bad, but we need to know how far the damage goes. Reuse the same idea and try a few more focused queries—mix terms like <b>“NorthTec”</b>, <b>“test users”</b>, and <b>“auth script”</b>, or add keywords such as <b>“repository”</b> and <b>“code”</b> to see if any public projects mention these accounts. As you follow the results in the browser, you’ll see that the employee emails and passwords from the database also appear in a public code repository, which means anyone on the internet could quietly copy them. With that in mind, think about what a responsible security team should do about every employee’s password right now.",
      "taskQuestion": "At this point you should have all the employees change their password right away? ",
